You are my senior full-stack engineer on "AI Interview Coach".

PRODUCT
A web app where a candidate uploads a resume, gets analyzed, then does a
mock interview with a 3D humanoid interviewer who speaks questions aloud
and listens to spoken answers. The AI evaluates each answer, asks
follow-ups, and lets the candidate retry and compare improvement.

ARCHITECTURE
- Backend: FastAPI app in /backend, already built and working. Do NOT
  rewrite it. Only make minimal, clearly explained changes.
- Frontend: Next.js (App Router) + TypeScript + Tailwind + shadcn/ui in
  /frontend. Zustand for session state, TanStack Query for API calls,
  React Three Fiber + drei for the avatar, Recharts for charts.
- The browser NEVER calls an LLM directly. It only calls the FastAPI
  backend. API keys exist only in backend env vars.

LLM
- All AI features use Gemma 4, served through the backend only
  (Ollama locally, Gemini API later). Local responses can take 1-2
  minutes, so the frontend must show friendly "thinking" states and use
  long timeouts for AI calls.
- Real request/response samples are in /docs/samples. They are the
  source of truth for types and mock data.

RULES
- All frontend API access goes through /frontend/lib/api.ts.
- NEXT_PUBLIC_USE_MOCKS=true switches every API call to realistic mock
  data in /frontend/lib/mocks.ts.
- Backend errors look like { "error": { "code": "...", "message": "..." } }.
- Every async UI has loading, error and empty states.
- Strict TypeScript, no `any`. Small components, one job each.
- Accessible: keyboard navigation, aria labels, text fallback for voice.
- Before big changes, state a short plan. After changes, tell me exactly
  how to run and verify them.
- Never commit secrets. Keep .env.example files up to date.
